# Copy to `.env` and fill in to turn analytics on.
# With PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY unset, analytics is a no-op and posthog-js is never
# downloaded by the browser — see src/lib/analytics.ts.

# Project API key from PostHog → Settings → Project.
# This key is public by design; it is embedded in the client bundle.
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=

# Defaults to `/ingest`, a first-party proxy path served by the rewrites in
# netlify.toml (which forward to the PostHog US cloud hosts). Leave unset in
# production.
#
# LOCAL DEV TRAP: `astro dev` does NOT apply netlify.toml redirects, so `/ingest`
# returns 404 locally and no events are sent. To test analytics locally, bypass the
# proxy by setting:
#   PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
# PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=

# Where the real PostHog app lives, so the toolbar and in-app links don't resolve
# against our own origin. Defaults to https://us.posthog.com (US cloud); there is
# normally no reason to set it.
# PUBLIC_POSTHOG_UI_HOST=
